# checkpatch WARNING types that do not fail the patch check.
#
# One type per line, then the reason it is accepted for our patches:
#   TYPE  reason
# Every entry is a decision against the kernel's own style rules and needs a
# reason that holds for every patch, not just the one that raised it.
# ERRORs cannot be allowed here; CHECKs never fail.
UNKNOWN_COMMIT_ID  the check tree is the kernel.org tarball plus the series, with no git history, so checkpatch can resolve no commit id; a Fixes: tag naming the upstream commit it fixes is what upstream asks for
